From 18a73d27819bd0277febb7871510c82711c03bbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:16:24 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 25/28] Host audio tracks: a host audio file played as one of
 the game's ATRAC tracks

host/audio/host_audio.hpp lets a port play an audio file of the host's
own (MP3, Ogg Vorbis, Opus, FLAC, WAV) where the game plays one of its
ATRAC3plus tracks, with no ATRAC encoding. A port registers a file and
its loop under a 32-bit id (register_host_track) and serves the game a
stand-in ATRAC3plus WAVE file for it (virtual_atrac_file), for example
through a file provider at the path the game opens. The stand-in carries
the track's length in `fact`, its loop in `smpl`, a private "PKHA" chunk
naming the id, and frames of zero bytes. sceAtrac (hle_atrac.cpp) reads
the chunk and fills each frame from the decoded file at the same
positions instead of opening the ATRAC decoder; the game's buffer and
reads, sceAtracAddStreamData, GetStreamDataInfo, loops and resets are the
same code as for the game's own tracks, so the game cannot tell.

Files are decoded with libavformat, libavcodec and libswresample to
44,100 Hz 16-bit stereo (downmixed or resampled as needed) the first time
they are needed, through the host's own file I/O, and kept in memory
while they play; the last three decoded stay cached, and
prefetch_host_track decodes on a worker thread. Loops: the whole file, a
range in samples of the file or in seconds, the file's own LOOPSTART with
LOOPLENGTH or LOOPEND tags, or none. Tracks over 30 minutes, unreadable
files and files with no decodable audio are refused with a log line.

A file without a PKHA chunk is handled exactly as before. With
<prefix>_NO_HOST_AUDIO set, or a build without libavformat, nothing is
registered, no stand-in is made and the chunk is ignored.

Verified on Windows with one game (recompiled, no interpreter): a
stand-in served in place of its battle music played a generated 6 s
WAV (in the whole-file case) and a 30 s WAV streamed in 16
AddStreamData calls, both looping at their loop points, checked in the
audio dump with a Goertzel scan; MP3, Vorbis (with loop tags), Opus
(48 kHz), FLAC and 48 kHz mono WAV decode at the right pitch and length.
Not verified: other games, the source-built FFmpeg, prefetch from a
game's menu, a track that plays once to its end in a game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
